---
export const prerender = true
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import DocCode from "../../../components/docs/DocCode.astro"
import DocRelated from "../../../components/docs/DocRelated.astro"
import ApiSchema from "../../../components/docs/ApiSchema.astro"
import { apiGroups } from "../../../data/apiGroups"
import { operationsFor, referencedSchemas, apiDocument, schemaAnchor, schemaType, schemaRules, requestExample } from "../../../lib/apiReference"
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return apiGroups.map((group) => ({ params: { group: group.slug }, props: { group } }))
}
const { group } = Astro.props
const entries = operationsFor(group)
const schemas = referencedSchemas(entries)
const toc = [
  { title: "Resource contract", href: "#overview" },
  { title: "Operations", href: "#operations" },
  ...entries.map((entry) => ({ title: entry.operation.operationId, href: `#${entry.anchor}`, depth: 3 })),
  ...(schemas.length ? [{ title: "Referenced schemas", href: "#schemas" }] : []),
  { title: "How to read this page", href: "#reading" },
  { title: "Calling this group from TypeScript", href: "#group-clients" },
  { title: "Troubleshooting requests", href: "#group-troubleshooting" },
]
---
<DocsLayout title={`${group.title} API`} subtitle={group.summary} description={`CADCAMFUN ${group.title.toLowerCase()} API: methods, paths, authentication, request fields, responses, errors, and schemas.`} toc={toc}>
  <section id="overview" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Resource contract</h2>
    <p>{entries.length} operations in the <code>{group.tag}</code> HttpApi group. Methods, paths, parameters, payload schemas, response status codes, and media types below come directly from the application's composed contract.</p>
    <p>Use the sidecar URL announced at startup as <code>CADCAMFUN_URL</code>. Protected operations take the application launch token in the <code>Authorization</code> header. Companion tokens and AI bridge tokens have narrower access; their presence does not grant access to this entire resource.</p>
    <p><a href={group.guide}>Read the related subsystem guide</a> for behavior and operational limits. <a href="/docs/api#authorization">API authentication</a> explains the account-session distinction. <a href="/docs/api/openapi.json">Download the complete OpenAPI document</a> for nested schemas and client generation.</p>
    <p>Request examples are templates: replace path and query placeholders, set the actual connection variables, and create a payload file matching the indicated media type and schema before submitting a write. Optional fields may still be required by a business rule; the contract describes transport validation.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="operations" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Operations</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Operation ID</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{entries.map((entry) => <tr><td><strong>{entry.method}</strong></td><td><a href={`#${entry.anchor}`}><code>{entry.path}</code></a></td><td><code>{entry.operation.operationId}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>
  {entries.map((entry) => <section id={entry.anchor} class="doc-section">
    <h2><code>{entry.operation.operationId}</code></h2>
    <p><strong>{entry.method}</strong> <code>{entry.path}</code></p>
    {entry.operation.summary && <p>{entry.operation.summary}</p>}
    {entry.operation.description && <p>{entry.operation.description}</p>}
    <p><strong>Authentication:</strong> {entry.operation.security?.length ? "Bearer token required." : "No bearer middleware is declared for this operation."} {entry.operation.deprecated && "This operation is marked deprecated."}</p>
    <h3>Parameters</h3>
    {(entry.operation.parameters?.length ?? 0) > 0 ? <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Location</th><th>Presence</th><th>Type and constraints</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{entry.operation.parameters!.map((parameter) => <tr>
        <td><code>{parameter.name}</code></td><td>{parameter.in}</td><td>{parameter.required ? "Required" : "Optional"}</td>
        <td><code>{schemaType(parameter.schema)}</code>{parameter.description && <p>{parameter.description}</p>}{schemaRules(parameter.schema) && <p>{schemaRules(parameter.schema)}</p>}</td>
      </tr>)}</tbody>
    </table></div> : <p>No path, query, or endpoint-specific header parameters are declared.</p>}
    <h3>Request body</h3>
    {entry.operation.requestBody ? <>
      <p>{entry.operation.requestBody.required ? "Required" : "Optional"} request body. Use one of the declared encodings.</p>
      {Object.entries(entry.operation.requestBody.content).map(([media, value]) => <>
        <h4><code>{media}</code></h4>
        {value.schema !== undefined ? <ApiSchema schema={value.schema} title="Request schema" /> : <p>No body schema is declared for this encoding.</p>}
      </>)}
    </> : <p>No request body is declared.</p>}
    <h3>Responses</h3>
    {Object.entries(entry.operation.responses).map(([status, response]) => <>
      <h4><code>{status}</code> — {response.description ?? "Response"}</h4>
      {response.headers && <p>Response headers: {Object.keys(response.headers).map((header) => <code>{header} </code>)}</p>}
      {Object.keys(response.content ?? {}).length ? Object.entries(response.content!).map(([media, value]) => <>
        <p><strong>Content type:</strong> <code>{media}</code></p>
        {value.schema !== undefined ? <ApiSchema schema={value.schema} title={`Response ${status} schema`} /> : <p>This media type has no declared JSON schema.</p>}
      </>) : <p>No response body schema is declared.</p>}
    </>)}
    <h3>Request template</h3>
    {entry.operation.requestBody?.content["multipart/form-data"] ? <p>This operation uses multipart form data. Build form parts according to its schema using the client upload API or <code>curl --form</code>; do not set a multipart boundary manually.</p> : <DocCode language="bash" title="Connection and payload placeholders">{requestExample(entry)}</DocCode>}
  </section>)}
  {schemas.length > 0 && <section id="schemas" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Referenced schemas</h2>
    <p>These named schemas are reachable from this resource's parameters, payloads, and responses. Optional presence and nullable values are different: a required field can explicitly accept <code>null</code>.</p>
    {schemas.map((name) => <section id={schemaAnchor(name)}>
      <h3><code>{name}</code></h3>
      <ApiSchema schema={apiDocument.components.schemas[name]!} title={name} />
    </section>)}
  </section>}
    <section id="reading" class="doc-section">
    <h2>How to read this page</h2>
    <p>Each operation section below has the same parts: method and path, authentication, a parameter table, request body schema per media type, one block per declared response status, and a request template. The schema viewer shows required fields, optional fields, nullable values and constraints such as minimum length or enumerations.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>You see</th><th>It means</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Required</td><td>The field or parameter must be present. It may still accept <code>null</code> if its type says so.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Optional</td><td>May be omitted. The handler can still reject the request for business reasons.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>_tag</code> in an error schema</td><td>The discriminator of the tagged error. Switch on it in clients.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Several 4xx schemas for one status</td><td>The status is shared by different failure families; decode by <code>_tag</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>No response body schema</td><td>An empty body, such as 204, or a body that is not JSON.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="group-clients" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Calling this group from TypeScript</h2>
    <p>In the generated Promise SDK, operations of this group live under the client namespace named after the group, and in the Effect client under <code>api.{group.tag}</code>. Operation IDs on this page have the form <code>{group.tag}.&lt;name&gt;</code>; the part after the dot is the method name in both clients.</p>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Promise SDK">
{"import { CadCam, ClientError } from \"@cadcamfun/api/sdk\"\n\nconst client = CadCam.make({\n  baseUrl: process.env.CADCAMFUN_URL!,\n  headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.CADCAMFUN_TOKEN}` },\n})\n\ntry {\n  // e.g. client.projects.list(), client.projects.get({ id })\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof ClientError) {\n    // Transport | UnexpectedStatus | UnsupportedContentType | MalformedResponse | SseEventTooLarge\n  } else {\n    // a declared error body: switch on error._tag\n  }\n}"}
    </DocCode>
    <p>A declared failure is thrown as the decoded JSON body itself, not wrapped. Anything outside the declared statuses becomes <code>ClientError("UnexpectedStatus")</code>. Network failures and aborts become <code>ClientError("Transport")</code> with the cause folded into the message.</p>
    <p>A few operations with multipart uploads, binary or JavaScript responses, raw webhooks, or colliding input names are not generated. Use the full Effect <code>ApiClient</code> or <code>fetch</code> for those.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="group-troubleshooting" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting requests</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>401 on every call</td><td>Token from a previous launch, or missing <code>Bearer</code> prefix</td><td>Read the current token from the desktop connection; send <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>400 before anything happens</td><td>Body or parameter does not match the schema</td><td>Compare the payload with the request schema above; check types, enumerations and required fields.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>403 or 404 on a record you can see elsewhere</td><td>The acting account differs (session header absent or expired)</td><td>Send the right <code>x-session-token</code>, or use the local profile that owns the record.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>409</td><td>A conflicting state, such as a duplicate name or stale branch head</td><td>Re-read the resource and retry with current data.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Connection refused</td><td>The sidecar restarted on a new port</td><td>Resolve the URL again; ports are not stable between launches.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <DocRelated items={[{ title: "API overview", href: "/docs/api" }, { title: "Subsystem guide", href: group.guide }, { title: "Local development", href: "/docs/guides/local-dev" }]} />
</DocsLayout>
